{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"85f50071-007c-4501-9922-a5db12bbca9b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented the fix so that heart‑rate corridors are generated in **absolute BPM** instead of the watch’s own zone percentages.\n\n**Key changes**\n- Added a constant `LTHR = 172` (the athlete’s lactate‑threshold heart rate) after the imports.  \n- Re‑implemented `hr_target` to convert the planned `%LTHR` range to BPM using that constant and return `{ \"units\": \"bpm\", \"value\": lo_bpm, \"end\": hi_bpm }`.  \n- Cleaned up duplicate `LTHR` definitions and added explanatory comments.\n\nThese adjustments ensure the generated `workout_doc` contains the exact BPM ranges we planned, eliminating the watch‑specific zone truncation seen in `watch‑notes.md`.\n\nYou can review the updated generator and the summary of changes here:\n\n- [gen.py](file:///tmp/h-uPXLlC/gen.py)  \n- [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-uPXLlC/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":140.166987,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":28975,"output_tokens":12533,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":403648,"total_tokens":41508}}}
